Message-Id: <8303ed2ce51ece61ca2cec0bdf6557b4e7e8b99d.1795068663.git.dev@kobbler.invalid>
In-Reply-To: <7569a748d6d008513cbf39061bc4db416ff59617.1795068663.git.dev@kobbler.invalid>
References: <7569a748d6d008513cbf39061bc4db416ff59617.1795068663.git.dev@kobbler.invalid>
From: Kobbler-Media <dev@kobbler.invalid>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 17:10:54 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] demux: mkv: do not take a discardable picture's PTS for
 its DTS

Matroska stores no DTS, so a video block's DTS is taken as its PTS for a
keyframe, and for any other picture as the PTS capped at a frame after
the last DTS. A discardable picture also got its PTS, on the grounds that
nothing refers to it so it is shown as soon as it is decoded. That does
not hold in a B-pyramid, where pictures decoded after it can be shown
before it: some muxers flag those discardable too.

Its DTS then lands ahead of the pictures that follow it, and as the PCR
is the lowest DTS of the tracks, the PCR jumps ahead with it and stalls
until they catch up. An episode muxed that way put the PCR 240ms ahead of
its video at every such picture, so the PCR came in bursts of up to
360ms, enough for the input clock to take each burst for a gap in the
stream.

A discardable picture now gets the same DTS as any other picture that is
not a keyframe, which for a B-frame of a plain GOP is its PTS anyway.
With no default duration to step by, it still gets its PTS.
---
 modules/demux/mkv/mkv.cpp |   9 +-
 test/Makefile.am          |   3 +
 test/modules/demux/mkv.c  | 188 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 test/modules/meson.build  |   8 ++
 4 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 test/modules/demux/mkv.c

diff --git a/modules/demux/mkv/mkv.cpp b/modules/demux/mkv/mkv.cpp
index a6a5abd5c7..f752d86023 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mkv/mkv.cpp
+++ b/modules/demux/mkv/mkv.cpp
@@ -788,10 +788,11 @@ static void BlockDecode( demux_t *p_demux, KaxBlock *block, KaxSimpleBlock *simp
             else
             {
                 p_block->i_pts = i_pts;
-                // condition when the DTS is correct (keyframe or B frame == NOT P frame)
-                if ( b_key_picture || b_discardable_picture )
-                        p_block->i_dts = p_block->i_pts;
-                else if ( track.i_last_dts == VLC_TICK_INVALID )
+                /* A discardable picture can still be shown after pictures
+                 * decoded after it, as in a B-pyramid: its PTS is not its DTS
+                 * then, and would put the PCR ahead of them. */
+                if ( b_key_picture || track.i_last_dts == VLC_TICK_INVALID ||
+                     ( b_discardable_picture && !track.i_default_duration ) )
                     p_block->i_dts = i_pts;
                 else
                     p_block->i_dts = std::min( i_pts, track.i_last_dts + track.i_default_duration );
